#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:148
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Seamonkey"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:151
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The configuration of <application>Seamonkey</application> is accomplished by"
" creating a <filename>mozconfig</filename> file containing the desired "
"configuration options. A default <filename>mozconfig</filename> file is "
"created below. To see the entire list of available configuration options "
"(and an abbreviated description of each one), issue <command>python3 "
"configure.py --help</command>. You may also wish to review the entire file "
"and uncomment any other desired options. Create the file by issuing the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""

#.  With Firefox ESR 128 we'd replace the following part with
#. "- -enable-elf-hack=relr", or remove it if relr becomes the default.
#. But I've no idea if SeaMonkey will have this change backported.
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:161
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<?dbfo keep-together=\"auto\"?><userinput>cat &gt; mozconfig &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># If you have a multicore machine, all cores will be used\n"
"\n"
"# If you have installed DBus-Glib comment out this line:\n"
"ac_add_options --disable-dbus\n"
"\n"
"# If you have installed dbus-glib, and you have installed (or will install)\n"
"# wireless-tools, and you wish to use geolocation web services, comment out\n"
"# this line\n"
"ac_add_options --disable-necko-wifi\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"# If you wish to use libproxy to determine proxy server information, you will\n"
"# need to install the libproxy package and then uncomment the option below:\n"
"#ac_add_options --enable-libproxy\n"
"\n"
"# Uncomment these lines if you have installed optional dependencies:\n"
"#ac_add_options --enable-system-hunspell\n"
"\n"
"# Uncomment the following option if you have not installed PulseAudio\n"
"#ac_add_options --disable-pulseaudio\n"
"# and uncomment this if you installed alsa-lib instead of PulseAudio\n"
"#ac_add_options --enable-alsa\n"
"\n"
"# Comment out following options if you have not installed\n"
"# recommended dependencies:\n"
"ac_add_options --with-system-icu\n"
"ac_add_options --with-system-libevent\n"
"ac_add_options --with-system-nspr\n"
"ac_add_options --with-system-nss\n"
"ac_add_options --with-system-webp\n"
"\n"
"# Disabling debug symbols makes the build much smaller and a little\n"
"# faster. Comment this if you need to run a debugger.\n"
"ac_add_options --disable-debug-symbols\n"
"\n"
"# The elf-hack is reported to cause failed installs (after successful builds)\n"
"# on some machines. It is supposed to improve startup time and it shrinks\n"
"# libxul.so by a few MB.  With recent Binutils releases the linker already\n"
"# supports a much safer and generic way for this.\n"
"ac_add_options --disable-elf-hack\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-linker=bfd\n"
"export LDFLAGS=\"$LDFLAGS -Wl,-z,pack-relative-relocs\"\n"
"\n"
"# Seamonkey has some additional features that are not turned on by default,\n"
"# such as an IRC client, calendar, and DOM Inspector. The DOM Inspector\n"
"# aids with designing web pages. Comment these options if you do not\n"
"# desire these features.\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-calendar\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-dominspector\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-irc\n"
"\n"
"# The BLFS editors recommend not changing anything below this line:\n"
"ac_add_options --prefix=/usr\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-application=comm/suite\n"
"\n"
"ac_add_options --disable-crashreporter\n"
"ac_add_options --disable-updater\n"
"ac_add_options --disable-tests\n"
"\n"
"# The SIMD code relies on the unmaintained packed_simd crate which\n"
"# fails to build with Rustc >= 1.78.0.  We may re-enable it once\n"
"# Mozilla ports the code to use std::simd and std::simd is stabilized.\n"
"ac_add_options --disable-rust-simd\n"
"\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-strip\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-install-strip\n"
"\n"
"# You cannot distribute the binary if you do this.\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-official-branding\n"
"\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-system-ffi\n"
"ac_add_options --enable-system-pixman\n"
"ac_add_options --with-system-jpeg\n"
"ac_add_options --with-system-png\n"
"ac_add_options --with-system-zlib\n"
"\n"
"export CC=clang CXX=clang++</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:249
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"First, if you are building with system ICU, adapt the line break mapping for"
" ICU-74 or later, apply a patch to build this package with the C++17 "
"standard because the headers of ICU-75 or later require some C++17 features,"
" and adapt the build system to use the correct library with ICU-76 or later:"
msgstr ""

#.  This used to be 43..47. ICU-78 adjusted line mapping. Firefox 140esr is
#.      adjusted by adding a CLASS_CHARACTER at the end of what would be 47.
#. So we
#.      just increase 47 to 48 to adapt for ICU-78 rather quite easily instead
#. of
#.      needing another sed command/expression. May change again in ICU-79.
#.      - zeckma
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:261
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">(for i in {43..48}; do\n"
"   sed '/ZWJ/s/$/,CLASS_CHARACTER/' -i intl/lwbrk/LineBreaker.cpp || exit $?\n"
"done) &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"patch -Np1 -i ../seamonkey-&seamonkey-version;-cxx17-1.patch &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"sed -i 's/icu-i18n/icu-uc &amp;/' js/moz.configure</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:271
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Next, remove a hunk of unused code violating the C++ standard.  Clang has "
"started to reject it even though it's unused since the 19.1.0 release:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:276
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed -e '/ExclusiveData(ExclusiveData&amp;&amp;/,/^ *}/d' \\\n"
"    -i js/src/threading/ExclusiveData.h</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:280
#, xml-text
msgid "Next, fix a problem with the bundled 'distro' python module:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:283
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">sed -e '1012 s/stderr=devnull/stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL/' \\\n"
"    -e '1013 s/OSError/(OSError, subprocess.CalledProcessError)/' \\\n"
"    -i third_party/python/distro/distro.py</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:288
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Compile <application>Seamonkey</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:292
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>export PATH_PY311=/opt/python3.11/bin:$PATH &amp;&amp;\n"
"export MOZBUILD_STATE_PATH=${PWD}/mozbuild  &amp;&amp;\n"
"PATH=$PATH_PY311 AUTOCONF=true MACH_USE_SYSTEM_PYTHON=1 ./mach build</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:297
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:301
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Seamonkey</application> by issuing the following "
"commands as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:307
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If <command>sudo</command> or <command>su</command> is invoked for opening a"
" shell running as the &root; user, ensure <envar>PATH_PY311</envar> is "
"correctly passed or the following command will fail.  For "
"<command>sudo</command>, use the <option>--preserve-env=PATH_PY311</option> "
"option.  For <command>su</command>, do <emphasis>not</emphasis> use the "
"<option>-</option> or <option>--login</option> options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:317
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>PATH=$PATH_PY311 MACH_USE_SYSTEM_PYTHON=1 ./mach install &amp;&amp;\n"
"chown -R 0:0 /usr/lib/seamonkey                          &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cp -v $(find -name seamonkey.1 | head -n1) /usr/share/man/man1</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:323
#, xml-text
msgid "Finally, unset temporary variables that were set above:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:326
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>unset PATH_PY311 MOZBUILD_STATE_PATH</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:331
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:334
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>export MOZBUILD_STATE_PATH=${PWD}/mozbuild</command>: The build "
"tells you that it intends to create <filename "
"class=\"directory\">~/.mozbuild</filename>, and offer you an option to press"
" &lt;ENTER&gt; to accept this, or Ctrl-C to cancel and restart the build "
"after specifying the directory. In practice, the message may not appear "
"until after &lt;ENTER&gt; is keyed, i.e. the build stalls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:343
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"That directory is used for a (probably random) telemetry identifier.  "
"Creating this directory within the build directory and deleting it after the"
" installation prevents it being used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:349
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>export CC=clang CXX=clang++</command>: With the introduction of "
"<application>gcc-12</application>, many more warnings are generated when "
"compiling mozilla applications and that results in a much slower, and "
"larger, build. Furthermore, building with GCC on i?86 is currently broken.  "
"Although upstream mozilla code defaults to using "
"<application>llvm</application> unless overridden, the older configure code "
"in <application>Seamonkey</application> defaults to gcc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:374
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>./mach build --verbose</option>: Use this alternative if you need "
"details of which files are being compiled, together with any C or C++ flags "
"being used. But do not add '--verbose' to the install command, it is not "
"accepted there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:381
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>./mach build -jN</option>: The build should, by default, use all the"
" online CPU cores. If using all the cores causes the build to swap because "
"you have insufficient memory, using fewer cores can be faster."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:389
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Seamonkey"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:392
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For installing various <application>Seamonkey</application> add-ons, refer "
"to <ulink url=\"https://addons.thunderbird.net/en-US/seamonkey/\">Add-ons "
"for Seamonkey</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:398
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Along with using the <quote>Preferences</quote> menu to configure "
"<application>Seamonkey</application>'s options and preferences to suit "
"individual tastes, finer grain control of many options is only available "
"using a tool not available from the general menu system. To access this "
"tool, you'll need to open a browser window and enter <systemitem "
"role=\"url\">about:config</systemitem> in the address bar. This will display"
" a list of the configuration preferences and information related to each "
"one. You can use the <quote>Search:</quote> bar to enter search criteria and"
" narrow down the listed items. Changing a preference can be done using two "
"methods. One, if the preference has a boolean value (True/False), simply "
"double-click on the preference to toggle the value and two, for other "
"preferences simply right-click on the desired line, choose "
"<quote>Modify</quote> from the menu and change the value. Creating new "
"preference items is accomplished in the same way, except choose "
"<quote>New</quote> from the menu and provide the desired data into the "
"fields when prompted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:417
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you use a desktop environment like <application>Gnome</application> or "
"<application>KDE</application> you may wish to create a "
"<filename>seamonkey.desktop</filename> file so that "
"<application>Seamonkey</application> appears in the panel's menus. If you "
"didn't enable <application>Startup-Notification</application> in your "
"mozconfig change the StartupNotify line to false. As the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/xsoft/graphweb/seamonkey.xml:426
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir -pv /usr/share/{applications,pixmaps}              &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /usr/share/applications/seamonkey.desktop &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Encoding=UTF-8\n"
"Type=Application\n"
"Name=Seamonkey\n"
"Comment=The Mozilla Suite\n"
"Icon=seamonkey\n"
"Exec=seamonkey\n"
"Categories=Network;GTK;Application;Email;Browser;WebBrowser;News;\n"
"StartupNotify=true\n"
"Terminal=false</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"ln -sfv /usr/lib/seamonkey/chrome/icons/default/default128.png \\\n"
"        /usr/share/pixmaps/seamonkey.png</userinput>"
msgstr ""

